{"name":"Wonder Lust","hex":"#ef8e9f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wonder","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sense of awe, astonishment and curiosity, inspired by unexpected events, novel experiences and inexplicable circumstances, sometimes accompanied by surprise, shock or reverence.","Something that causes amazement or awe; a marvel."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be affected with surprise or admiration; to be struck with astonishment; to be amazed; to marvel; often followed by at.","To ponder; to feel doubt and curiosity; to query in the mind."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wonder"},{"term":"lust","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A feeling of strong desire, especially such a feeling driven by sexual arousal.","A general want or longing, not necessarily sexual."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To look at or watch with a strong desire, especially of a sexual nature.","To desire."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lust"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wonder (emotion)","blocks":[{"text":"Wonder is an emotion comparable to surprise that people feel when perceiving something rare or unexpected. It has historically been seen as an important aspect of human nature, specifically being linked with curiosity and the drive behind intellectual exploration. Wonder is also often compared to the emotion of awe but awe implies fear or respect rather than joy. Science fiction can produce a \"sense of wonder\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/I_Wonder.jpg/330px-I_Wonder.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wonder_(emotion)","wikidata":"Q977433"},{"title":"Lust","blocks":[{"text":"Lust is an intense desire for something. Lust can take any form such as the lust for sexual activity, money, or power; but it can also take such mundane forms as the lust for food or the lust for redolence. Lust is similar to, but distinguished from, passion, in that properly ordered passion propels individuals to achieve benevolent goals whilst lust does not."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Jheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_%28Luxuria%29.jpg/330px-Jheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_%28Luxuria%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lust","wikidata":"Q6498477"},{"title":"Shades of red","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color red may differ in hue, chroma, lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a red or other hue mixed with white, a shade being mixed with black. A large selection of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Shades_of_Red.svg/330px-Shades_of_Red.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_red","wikidata":"Q7460345"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Aspiration_by_Edmund_J._Sullivan.jpg/330px-Aspiration_by_Edmund_J._Sullivan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Aspiration_by_Edmund_J._Sullivan.jpg/330px-Aspiration_by_Edmund_J._Sullivan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Aspiration\" by E. J. Sullivan, 1898 illustration for Thomas Carlyle's Sartor Resartus","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAspiration_by_Edmund_J._Sullivan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Daemon.jpg/500px-Daemon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Daemon.jpg/500px-Daemon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A demon satiating his lust in a 13th-century manuscript","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADaemon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Sankt_Bartholom%C3%A4us_%28Reichenthal%29_04.jpg/500px-Sankt_Bartholom%C3%A4us_%28Reichenthal%29_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Sankt_Bartholom%C3%A4us_%28Reichenthal%29_04.jpg/1280px-Sankt_Bartholom%C3%A4us_%28Reichenthal%29_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Sankt_Bartholom%C3%A4us_%28Reichenthal%29_04.jpg/500px-Sankt_Bartholom%C3%A4us_%28Reichenthal%29_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Detail of Lust at the Sankt Bartholomäus church (Reichenthal), Pulpit (1894)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASankt_Bartholom%C3%A4us_(Reichenthal)_04.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Mujeres_riendo.jpg/500px-Mujeres_riendo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Mujeres_riendo.jpg/1280px-Mujeres_riendo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Mujeres_riendo.jpg/500px-Mujeres_riendo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Goya's Man Mocked by Two Women (Dos Mujeres y un hombre), c. 1820","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMujeres_riendo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/RGB_illumination.jpg/330px-RGB_illumination.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/